WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.908
Your teeth cut, tear and grind your food.

2
00:00:07.128 --> 00:00:10.704
Look after them, and keep
your whole body healthy too.

3
00:00:11.204 --> 00:00:16.730
Open wide. You have three kinds of teeth.
Each has a shape that fits its job.

4
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:21.176
At the front are the incisors.
They are flat, and they cut.

5
00:00:21.396 --> 00:00:25.204
Beside them are the canines.
They are pointed, and they tear.

6
00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:28.768
At the back are the molars,
big and wide, with bumps.

7
00:00:28.988 --> 00:00:32.471
Molars grind and mash your
food into small pieces.

8
00:00:32.691 --> 00:00:37.753
Bite an apple. The front teeth cut
a piece off. The back teeth chew it.

9
00:00:38.253 --> 00:00:42.664
A toothbrush is a tool. It only
works if you use it the right way.

10
00:00:42.884 --> 00:00:46.553
Brush twice a day: in the
morning, and before bed.

11
00:00:46.773 --> 00:00:50.349
Squeeze a pea-sized blob of
toothpaste onto the brush.

12
00:00:50.569 --> 00:00:56.467
Brush in small, gentle circles. Do
the front teeth, then the sides.

13
00:00:56.687 --> 00:01:00.681
Then the tops of the molars.
Keep going for two whole minutes.

14
00:01:01.181 --> 00:01:04.850
Germs are tiny living things.
They are too small to see.

15
00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:09.899
Sugar feeds the germs in your mouth.
Then they make holes in your teeth.

16
00:01:10.119 --> 00:01:13.602
Having sweets and fizzy drinks
every day can cause holes.

17
00:01:13.822 --> 00:01:16.330
Water and fruit are kinder to your teeth.

18
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:20.823
A treat now and then is fine.
Every day, all day, is not.

19
00:01:21.323 --> 00:01:26.477
Three things keep your body healthy:
good food, keeping clean, and moving.

20
00:01:26.697 --> 00:01:31.481
Your diet is everything you eat and
drink. Fruit and vegetables are good food.

21
00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:35.277
Wash your hands before you eat.
It keeps germs out of your mouth.

22
00:01:35.497 --> 00:01:40.651
Move every day. Run, play and climb!
It keeps your heart and muscles strong.

23
00:01:40.871 --> 00:01:44.819
Then rest. Drink water, and
have a good night's sleep.

24
00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:48.848
Being ill means your body
is not working as it should.

25
00:01:49.068 --> 00:01:53.573
Often, germs have got in. There
are signs you can see and feel.

26
00:01:53.793 --> 00:01:57.462
A hot forehead is a fever.
You may feel shivery.

27
00:01:57.682 --> 00:02:02.976
A cough, a runny nose, or feeling
very tired. These are signs too.

28
00:02:03.196 --> 00:02:06.818
Do not hide it. Tell a grown-up,
so you get better sooner.

29
00:02:07.038 --> 00:02:09.685
Rest and drink water. Your body will mend.

30
00:02:10.185 --> 00:02:14.179
Incisors cut, canines
tear, and molars grind.

31
00:02:14.399 --> 00:02:18.346
Brush twice a day for two minutes,
and have sweets less often.

32
00:02:18.566 --> 00:02:22.282
Good food, keeping clean and
moving keep your body healthy.

33
00:02:22.502 --> 00:02:25.892
If you feel ill, tell a
grown-up. Your body will mend.
